    {
      "name": "DPP 07",
      "displayName": "DPP 07",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "6970815ba0bee0d5d413be04",
          "question": "<p>The potential energy of a particle of mass \\( m \\) executing SHM is given by \\( U=A(1-\\cos 2 x) \\), where \\( x \\) is the instantaneous small displacement of the particle. The time period of oscillation is</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{m}{A}} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{m}{A}} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{m}{2 A}} \\)</p>",
            "<p>&nbsp;\\( 2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{m}{2 A}} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "6970815ba0bee0d5d413be30",
          "question": "<p>A uniform rod of length \\( l \\) is suspended at \\( l / 4 \\) from one end and made to undergo small oscillations. The time period of oscillation is:</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( 2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{7 l}{12 g}} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{3 l}{7 g}} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{7 l}{3 g}} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{4 l}{5 g}} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "6970815ba0bee0d5d413be07",
          "question": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Two particles are in SHM in a straight line. Amplitude \\( A \\) and time period \\( T \\) of both the&nbsp;particles are equal. At time \\( t=0 \\), one particle is at displacement \\( Y_{1}=+A \\) and the other at \\( Y_{2}=-\\frac{A}{2} \\), and they are approaching towards each other. After what time they cross each other?</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( T / 3 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( T / 4 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 5 T / 6 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( T / 6 \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 3,
          "explanation": "<p>Let both have amplitude (A) and angular frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>\n<p>Take particle 1 at the right extreme:</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>]</mo></math></p>\n<p>Particle 2 has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>cos</mi><msub><mi>&#981;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#981;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mtext>&#160;or&#160;</mtext><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.<br />&ldquo;Approaching each other&rdquo; requires <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> (to the right) while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> then leftward soon after, hence choose <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>&#981;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>:</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>]</mo></math></p>\n<p>They meet when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math>:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></math>[<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow><mi>&#969;</mi></mfrac></math>.<br /><br />Smallest (t&gt;0) is for (n=1): <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></math>.</p>"
        },
